From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 06:06:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: exynos9820-beyond2lte: Run the codec bus
 at 25 MHz

The codec bus started at 5 MHz until the SPI clock had been checked on
the phone.  At 5 MHz the source clock of the USI block reads 20 MHz, the
bus rate times the fixed divider of 4, set exactly from its 200 MHz
parent.  25 MHz, the rate of the vendor tree, needs 100 MHz, which the
same divider also reaches exactly.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
index 7240dff0f47..e348451d9b9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
@@ -691,7 +691,7 @@ &spi_2 {
 	audio-codec@0 {
 		compatible = "cirrus,cs47l93";
 		reg = <0>;
-		spi-max-frequency = <5000000>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <25000000>;
 
 		interrupts-extended = <&gpa2 2 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		interrupt-controller;
